[TEXT] **Root cause found.** Router6's FORWARD chain has explicit DROP rules for all traffic entering on **eth2** (the WAN uplink to router3):

```
iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 ACCEPT  ← lone exception
iifname "eth2" tcp → DROP  (0 pkts)
iifname "eth2" udp → DROP  (15 pkts = the probe pings!)
iifname "eth2" all → DROP  (24 pkts = ICMP from traceroutes!)
```

The counters prove active drops. Router6 can self-originate pings to pc16 (not subject to FORWARD), but all *forwarded* packets arriving from the WAN (router3 side) are silently dropped. This kills pc4→pc16 in the forward direction, AND kills pc15→pc12 on the return trip (pc12's reply re-enters router6 via eth2 and is dropped).

